<title>BELGIUM: EU COMMITTEE NOT SEEN DISCUSSING FINLAND AND ERM.</title>
<headline>EU COMMITTEE NOT SEEN DISCUSSING FINLAND AND ERM.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's monetary committee is not likely to discuss the issue of possible Finnish membership of the exchange rate mechanism ERM at its two-day meeting which ends on Tuesday, officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>Asked whether the committee would discuss the issue, Finland's Johnny Akerholm, permanent under-secretary of state at the finance ministry, told Reuters: &quot;Hardly...it is not topical.&quot;</p>
<p>Another EU monetary official said he could not imagine that the issue would be discussed at the meeting, which among other things will deal with a budget stability pact for countries joining a future economic and monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>The Finnish government has repeatedly said it will decide this autumn whether to link the markka to the ERM.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
</text>
